{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_3","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"cd /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-15_18-00-28-hashicorp_raft-real-run/draft && python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\nu={\n\\\"rationale\\\":\\\"Measured account of the live-cluster half of this question, replacing the source-derived statement that stood here. A new receipt (e52401f293244c72ae4e1dcb5f6889dd, experiment 22f697118ada4953a996e59b24685f31-experiment, events 37 and 38) restarts one follower of a three-voter commit-tracked cluster with RestoreCommittedLogs and then watches that node inside the live cluster. Setup event: three voters in force, the follower's staged commit index 9 and last log index 10. Restart event: the node came back with an empty recovered configuration, no leader, term 2, and the serving leader absent from its recovered configuration. Convergence event (37, comparison holds): the serving leader's heartbeats restored the node's leader view (recorded leader equals the serving leader), a command committed after the restart was stored by the node (last log index 10 to 11), the node stayed a follower and never campaigned, and its configuration stayed empty, so heartbeats and entries do not repair it. Outsider event (38, both comparisons violated): one AppendEntries request with no entries, sent by a server that appears in no configuration with the node's term plus five, was accepted, the outsider became the node's leader, the node's term rose to 7, and the serving leader of the healthy three-voter cluster stepped down, with no leader present at the moment of the event. The consequence is therefore measured rather than argued: a node recovered with RestoreCommittedLogs and an empty configuration gives a server that is in no configuration a way to raise the cluster's term and cost it its serving leader, while the entry and vote admissions recorded earlier remain as measured.\\\",\n\\\"interpretations\\\":[{\n \\\"investigation_id\\\":\\\"7e10640e7212486b94a80f04b69febc2-question-1\\\",\n \\\"experiment_id\\\":\\\"9d28f043326440548185371b0d4f375a-experiment\\\",\n \\\"source_ids\\\":[\\\"s-runfollower\\\",\\\"s-appendentries-stage\\\",\\\"s-restore-committed\\\",\\\"s-commit-tracking-contract\\\"],\n \\\"executions\\\":{\\\"7e6d5b3d49464a84ba43f7f9305ea5b6\\\":[19,20,21],\\\"e87ee87274544b3ba836dffb93a7ecb1\\\":[19,20],\\\"f418b9d6ab8841faa9ab6c35ce1fcd75\\\":[6,7],\\\"e1ee764584564a95b3e288381dfb75d9\\\":[6,7],\\\"e52401f293244c72ae4e1dcb5f6889dd\\\":[37,38]},\n \\\"joint_history\\\":\\\"Five receipts now answer this question from one recovery state, an empty configuration after a RestoreCommittedLogs restart. Two runs state the vote and pre-vote admission (f418b9d6ab8841faa9ab6c35ce1fcd75 and e1ee764584564a95b3e288381dfb75d9 at indices 6 and 7), one states the leadership acceptance and the election-gating control in a single-node cluster (e87ee87274544b3ba836dffb93a7ecb1 at indices 19 and 20), one states the entry path (7e6d5b3d49464a84ba43f7f9305ea5b6 at indices 19, 20 and 21), and the newest run (e52401f293244c72ae4e1dcb5f6889dd at indices 37 and 38) states the same behaviour inside a live three-voter cluster, where only the outsider contact is now measured rather than argued.\\\",\n \\\"rationale\\\":\\\"Current account: an empty recovered configuration removes participation checks on every path the question covers, while the node's own participation is gated off, and in a live cluster the node both converges on the legitimate leader and remains usable to an outsider. Measured in the newest receipt (e52401f293244c72ae4e1dcb5f6889dd at events 37 and 38): after the restart the node held an empty configuration with no leader; the serving leader's heartbeats restored its leader view and it stored a command committed after the restart (log index 10 to 11) while its configuration stayed empty and it stayed a follower; then one AppendEntries request with no entries from a server that appears in no configuration, carrying the node's term plus five, was accepted, the outsider became the node's leader, the node's term rose to 7 and the serving leader of the healthy three-voter cluster stepped down with no leader present at that moment. Mechanism from source: appendEntries applies no membership test to the sender and records it as leader while adopting its term, and the follower loop only clears a known leader when contact stops, so heartbeat contact from the legitimate leader converges the node's leader view but does not repair the configuration; an arriving configuration entry is the repair path measured elsewhere. Vote and pre-vote admission and the entry path stay as recorded in the earlier receipts.\\\",\n \\\"conclusion\\\":\\\"violated\\\",\n \\\"defect_claim\\\":\\\"asserted\\\",\n \\\"counterevidence\\\":[\n  \\\"The empty-list leniency in the vote handlers is intentional for cluster bootstrap, and appendEntries has always trusted the sender's identity; what makes both harmful here is that the node's own recovery produces an empty configuration in a cluster that is not being bootstrapped.\\\",\n  \\\"The measured outsider effect is a leadership change, not a log or data change: the outsider sent no entries and the node's log content was unchanged by that request, and the request itself is a legal protocol message rather than a forged one.\\\",\n  \\\"The node's own election gating is intact, so the failure is asymmetric: it admits others while suppressing itself, which also means it cannot repair the configuration by winning an election.\\\",\n  \\\"Convergence bound measured in the same receipt: because the legitimate leader kept heartbeating, the node's recorded leader was restored to that leader, so the outsider effect needs a sender that reaches the node while the legitimate leader is quiet, which is the ordering the probe created.\\\"],\n \\\"limitations\\\":[\n  \\\"Measured with the repository's in-memory transport and stores; production transports, authentication and network behaviour are not covered, and the outsider needed only transport reachability.\\\",\n  \\\"The entry phase used one command entry with no configuration semantics, so the FSM effect recorded is a single applied command.\\\",\n  \\\"The probe does not measure how long the empty configuration persists in a cluster without membership traffic; that follows from the repair path rather than from a timed observation.\\\",\n  \\\"The live-cluster run uses one three-voter in-memory cluster with timers shortened to 200 ms, one restarted follower and one outsider request; whether the cluster recovered a leader after the displacement was not measured, and the term the outsider could impose through a single quiet window is not bounded in time.\\\"]\n}]}\nopen('update.json','w').write(json.dumps(u,indent=2)+\\\"\\\\n\\\")\nprint('written')\nPY\n/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/.venv/bin/python -I -B -c \\\"import sys; sys.path.insert(0,'/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/src'); from consensus_assurance.cli import main; raise SystemExit(main())\\\" validate --run /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-15_18-00-28-hashicorp_raft-real-run --submission update.json 2>&1 | tail -3; date -u\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
